From 357f4c55d4ce83ec803d0800ecaafe240b64f2f9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yzddmr6 <46088090+yzddmr6@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 13:56:50 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] temperature: Add a grouped hwmon sensor view

Discover hwmon temperature channels on the refresh worker and display
current readings with expandable history in a Temperature sidebar page.
Use device names and channel labels, numeric channel ordering and the
existing temperature unit setting. Keep unreadable channels as N/A and
retain surviving sensors' history when devices are added or removed.
Allow autoscaled graphs to show negative temperatures.

Test discovery with synthetic hwmon devices, missing labels, numeric
ordering, negative and zero readings, faults, read errors, recovery,
removal and class symlinks.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
